# Every text file is stored with LF and checked out with LF, on Windows too, so a working tree's
# CRLF stops reaching other machines. A file already stored with CRLF is left as it is.
* text=auto eol=lf
# Shell scripts keep LF on a Windows checkout too: the release workflow runs them under Git Bash.
*.sh text eol=lf
packaging/linux/AppRun text eol=lf
# Generated and compared byte for byte by a chatd test (include_str!), so it must not become CRLF.
docs/parity.md text eol=lf
